# DineAI Prompt Engineering Framework Implementation Plan

Implement a decoupled, enterprise-grade prompt engineering framework in [prompts.py](file:///d:/data/AI_WAITER/dine_ai/llm/prompts.py). The framework will assemble, validate, optimize, localize, and manage the token budget of prompt components before they are sent to an LLM. It conforms strictly to SOLID, Clean Architecture, and patterns like Builder, Strategy, and Registry.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The prompt framework functions as a pipeline:
> 1. Components represent specific logical sections (System, Safety, Persona, Context, Memory).
> 2. The `PromptBuilder` retrieves a template, applies user configuration (language, persona, context), and chains sections based on priority.
> 3. The `PromptOptimizer` and `TokenBudgetManager` enforce strict length boundaries and apply context compression strategies (Top-K, Summarization, Metadata trimming) if the token limit is exceeded.
> 4. The output is a `PromptResult` containing execution metadata, a unique prompt hash, statistics, and validation warnings.

